+
+## Implementation Notes
+
+### Migration strategy
+This is a breaking change in file layout but NOT in CLI interface. All `kspec session` commands work identically — only the underlying storage location changes. The legacy fallback ensures existing sessions remain readable during transition.
+
+### Ordering (enforced by depends_on)
+1. Schema config (foundation)
+2. Path resolution (depends on schema) + spec updates (parallel)
+3. Remove shadow commits (depends on path resolution)
+4. Init/setup updates (depends on schema)
+5. Legacy fallback (depends on path resolution)
+6. Tests (depends on path resolution + shadow commit removal)
+7. Migration command (depends on legacy fallback)
+8. Branch mode last (post-mvp, depends on path resolution + init/setup)
+
+### Existing spec updates required
+These specs have ACs that hardcode `.kspec/sessions/` or inherit `@trait-shadow-commit`:
+- `@session-events` — ac-1, ac-7, ac-8 reference old paths/commit behavior
+- `@session-creation-and-env-injection` — ac-create, ac-budget-local, description reference old paths
+- `@session-log-list` — ac-1 references old path in given clause
+- `@session-compact` — inherits `@trait-shadow-commit` (remove binding)
+- `@session-stale-cleanup` — inherits `@trait-shadow-commit` (remove binding)
+- `@cli-ralph` — ac-22 references old tool-output path
+
+### Specs reviewed, no AC text changes needed
+- `@session-end-loop-signal` — doesn't hardcode paths; implementation uses path resolver
+- `@agent-invocation-lifecycle` — doesn't hardcode paths; in-progress implementation should use new resolver
+
+### Risk: daemon session routes
+The daemon builds from `dist/` not `src/` — session route changes need a daemon rebuild. Coordinate with existing daemon build pipeline.
+
+### Budget files
+Already local-only — no changes needed. They naturally move with the session directory.
